<title>USA: Mobil cancels spot purchase of Iraq crude.</title>
<headline>Mobil cancels spot purchase of Iraq crude.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mobil Corp N said Friday that it had cancelled a spot purchase of Iraqi crude from trading company Bayoil because of delays in shipping it to the U.S.</p>
<p>The contract, for part of a two million-barrel cargo of Basrah Light, was the first spot sale of Iraqi crude to the U.S. since sanctions were imposed in August, 1990.</p>
<p>&quot;We had made a contract with Bayoil for 500,000 barrels which was on the (Very Large Crude Carrier) Leonidas and were to take title when it lightered in the U.S. Gulf,&quot; said a Mobil official.</p>
<p>&quot;We were advised that it would be delayed for a substantial period that fell outside that agreed in the contract and therefore the contract was cancelled,&quot; he added.</p>
</text>
